From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaiyin Zhong <kaiyin@zhong.science>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:35:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] d3d12: on-disk shader cache for GLSL programs and
 pipeline states

d3d12 had no shader cache at all, so every process linked all of its GLSL
programs again and had the GPU driver compile all of its pipelines again. On
WSL with an Intel GPU a GTK 4 window's first frame took ~1.4 s, every time.

- Create a disk cache per screen (identity: Mesa build id, adapter ids, driver
  version, D3D12_DEBUG) and return it from get_disk_shader_cache, which turns
  on st/mesa's cache of linked programs (and GL_ARB_get_program_binary).
- Store driver-compiled graphics pipeline states (GetCachedBlob) in the same
  cache, keyed by the whole pipeline description with shader bytecode and the
  root signature key; the runtime validates a cached blob, and a rejected one
  is simply compiled again and replaced.

GTK 4 window, warm cache: first frame ~200 ms instead of ~1.4 s; output
pixel-identical to an uncached run.

Generated-by: LLM
